This optimization is designed for speeding up find_set . If we call find_set(v) for some vertex v , we actually find the representative p for all vertices that we visit on the path between v and the actual representative p . The trick is to make the paths for all those nodes shorter, by setting the parent of each visited vertex directly to p . You can see the operation in the following image. On the left there is a tree, and on the right side there is the compressed tree after calling find_set(7) , which shortens the paths for the visited nodes 7, 5, 3 and 2. The new implementation of find_set is as follows:

